Value Filldown VRF (\S+)
Value Required NEIGHBOR (\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+|[0-9a-fA-F]*:[0-9a-fA-F:.]+(?:%\S+)?)

# A peer is listed here exactly when it is activated for this family, in any state (feature 010,
# research R2). When a peer of the device has a description, a Description column comes first, so
# the neighbour is found as the address before the BGP version and the AS. Only the address is read.
# A link-local peer keeps its zone (fe80::1%Et1), as the neighbour view prints it.
# Any other line fails the step, a "%" line included, so a line this template cannot read never
# passes for a peer not activated for this family (issue #45). "% BGP inactive" alone never reaches
# the template: the step's empty_lines take it.
Start
  ^BGP summary information for VRF ${VRF}$$
  ^\s+(.*\s)?${NEIGHBOR}\s+4\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+ -> Record
  ^Router identifier \S+, local AS number \d+$$
  ^Neighbor Status Codes: .*$$
  ^\s+(Description\s+)?Neighbor\s+V\s+AS\s+MsgRcvd\s+MsgSent\s+InQ\s+OutQ\s+Up/Down\s+State\s+PfxRcd\s+PfxAcc\s+PfxAdv\s*$$
  ^\s*$$
  ^. -> Error
